Observability: AI Execution

Purpose:
  Define observability requirements specific to AI execution within
  the SDDRA system. Covers decision provenance, context tracking,
  cost tracking, token efficiency, tool/agent/skill performance,
  event architecture, audit trails, and budget enforcement.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Decision trace and provenance
  Context trace and snapshots
  Policy trace and snapshots
  AI execution fingerprint
  Cost tracking per task/agent/skill
  Token efficiency metrics
  Tool performance metrics
  Agent performance metrics
  Skill performance metrics
  Event architecture (event bus, envelope, versioning)
  Correlation and causation IDs
  Data classification and secret redaction
  Budget policy and alerting
  Root cause analysis and failure taxonomy
  Observability feedback loop

Principles:
  AI decision provenance MUST be reproducible.
  System records decision summary, not full chain-of-thought.
  Sensitive data MUST be redacted in all observability outputs.
  Observability data MUST be classified.
  Cost and token metrics are required for AI operations.
  Skill performance drives improvement decisions.
  Unknown execution result is NOT failure.

DecisionTrace:
  definition:
    record of why AI made a specific decision

  structure:
    decision:
      type: DATABASE_SELECTION
      candidates: [PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB]
      selected: PostgreSQL
      constraints: ACID required, relational model required
      source: ADR-012
      factors: [relational_data, transaction_support, existing_stack]

  rule: records summary and factors, not full chain-of-thought
  rule: enables reproducibility

ContextTrace:
  definition:
    record of what context was used for a task

  structure:
    context:
      task: TASK-100
      files: [user.go, repository.go]
      docs: [auth.md]
      decisions: [ADR-12]
      policies: [SEC-01]

  rule: context trace is recorded with execution

PolicyTrace:
  definition:
    record of which policies were evaluated and their decisions

  structure:
    policy_snapshot: POLICY-SNAPSHOT-20
    decisions:
      - policy: DEV-WRITE-01
        result: ALLOW
        reason: resource_in_write_scope

ContextSnapshot:
  definition:
    immutable snapshot of context at execution time

  structure:
    snapshot_id: CTX-100
    execution: EXEC-500
    sdd_version: 15
    source_revision: abc123
    items: [API-10, DOMAIN-AUTH, ARCH-5, auth/login.go]
    completeness: 1.0
    fingerprint: xyz789

PolicySnapshot:
  definition:
    immutable snapshot of active policies at execution time

  structure:
    snapshot_id: POLICY-SNAPSHOT-20
    execution: EXEC-500
    policies: [DEV-WRITE-01, SEC-AUTH-01, ...]

AIExecutionFingerprint:
  definition:
    hash of all execution dependencies for reproducibility

  structure:
    fingerprint:
      agent_version: 3.2.1
      skill_version: 2.1
      prompt_version: 7
      model_version: 1.5
      context_snapshot: CTX-100
      policy_snapshot: POLICY-SNAPSHOT-20

CostTracking:
  metrics:
    input_tokens
    output_tokens
    total_tokens
    estimated_cost

  example:
    EXEC-500:
      input = 120k
      output = 18k
      cost = $0.82

  cost_per_task:
    TASK-AUTH: average_cost = $0.31
    TASK-PAYMENT: average_cost = $2.80

  cost_per_agent:
    AGENT-CODER: $500/month
    AGENT-QA: $180/month
    AGENT-ARCHITECT: $220/month

  rule: cost MUST be tracked for all AI operations

TokenEfficiency:
  metric:
    task_success / token_usage

  rule: high token usage for simple tasks indicates skill/context problems
  rule: token efficiency is monitored and optimized

ToolPerformance:
  metrics:
    tool_calls_total
    tool_failures
    average_latency
    timeout_rate
    retry_rate

  example:
    go_test: failure_rate = 12%

AgentPerformance:
  metrics:
    success_rate
    failure_rate
    average_steps
    average_tokens
    average_cost
    average_duration
    retry_rate

SkillPerformance:
  metrics:
    success_rate
    average_duration
    failure_rate

  example:
    SKILL-REPOSITORY-PATTERN: success_rate = 96%
    SKILL-LEGACY-MIGRATION: success_rate = 61%

  rule: skill performance drives improvement decisions
  rule: low-performing skills are flagged for review

ObservabilityFeedbackLoop:
  flow:
    Execution -> Observability -> Metrics -> Analysis -> Skill Improvement -> New Version -> Execution

  rule: system can self-improve based on observability
  rule: auto-changes require governance approval

EventArchitecture:
  EventEnvelope:
    structure:
      event:
        id: string
        type: string
        version: string
        timestamp: ISO 8601
        correlation_id: string
        causation_id: string
        actor: string
        source: string
        payload: object

  EventVersioning:
    rule: event schemas are versioned
    rule: consumers handle old event versions

  EventBus:
    properties:
      ordering: per execution_id
      delivery: at-least-once
      retry: with exponential backoff
      dead-letter: DLQ for failed events
      idempotency: deduplication by event_id
      partitioning: by execution_id
      retention: configurable

  DuplicateEvents:
    rule: consumers MUST be idempotent
    rule: deduplication by event_id

  DeadLetterQueue:
    rule: failed events go to DLQ
    rule: DLQ is monitored and reprocessed

  Ordering:
    rule: ordering guaranteed per execution_id
    rule: global ordering NOT required

CorrelationCausation:
  CorrelationID:
    definition: links all events in a workflow
    example: CORR-500 flows through API -> Task -> Execution -> Agent -> Tool

  CausationID:
    definition: parent event that caused this event
    example: ToolCalled (caused_by: ExecutionStarted)

DataClassification:
  levels:
    PUBLIC: no restrictions
    INTERNAL: internal use only
    CONFIDENTIAL: restricted access
    SECRET: highly sensitive, never in plain text

  rule: all observability data MUST be classified
  rule: SECRET data is replaced with [REDACTED]

SecretRedaction:
  rule: secrets MUST be redacted in all outputs
  example:
    Authorization: Bearer eyJ... -> Authorization: [REDACTED]
    DATABASE_URL=postgres://... -> DATABASE_URL=[REDACTED]

  rule: observability system must not create security problems

BudgetPolicy:
  structure:
    budget:
      max_tokens: 200000
      max_cost: $2
      max_duration: 30m
      max_tool_calls: 100

  rule: budget exhaustion triggers PAUSE or DENY
  rule: budget policy is enforced by policy engine

EndToEndTrace:
  structure:
    REQ-100
      ↓
    TASK-200
      ↓
    EXEC-300
      ↓
    ├── AGENT-10
      │     ├── SKILL-20
      │     ├── CTX-30
      │     └── PROMPT-40
      ├── POLICY-50
      ├── ACTION-60
      │     └── TOOL-70
      ├── VALIDATION-80
      └── ARTIFACT-90

  rule: every node has ID, Version, Timestamp, Actor, Parent, Correlation

Provenance:
  definition:
    record of how a result was produced

  example:
    Artifact-90:
      created_by: EXEC-300
      derived_from: TASK-200
      implements: REQ-100

RootCauseAnalysis:
  flow:
    Task failed
      -> trace back through execution
      -> identify root cause
      -> example: root_cause = TOOL_TIMEOUT

FailureTaxonomy:
  categories:
    LLM_FAILURE
    TOOL_FAILURE
    NETWORK_FAILURE
    POLICY_DENIED
    VALIDATION_FAILURE
    TIMEOUT
    CONTEXT_FAILURE
    DEPENDENCY_FAILURE
    USER_INPUT_REQUIRED
    SYSTEM_FAILURE

  rule: failures are categorized, not just logged as errors

Alerting:
  ai_specific_alerts:
    - agent_retry_rate > 5
    - token_usage > expected_budget
    - execution_failure_rate > 20%
    - production_policy_denials > threshold

  rule: alerts are actionable and have owners

Navigation:
  Observability: @INDEX.sdd
  Logging: @logging.sdd
  Metrics: @metrics.sdd
  Tracing: @tracing.sdd
  Alerting: @alerting.sdd
  Health: @health.sdd
  Diagnostics: @diagnostics.sdd
  Incident: @incident.sdd
  Runtime: @../runtime/INDEX.sdd
  Execution: @../runtime/execution.sdd
  Events: @../runtime/events.sdd
  Architecture: @../architecture/observability.sdd

Rules:
  [AI-OBS-01] AI decision provenance MUST be reproducible.
  [AI-OBS-02] System records decision summary, not full chain-of-thought.
  [AI-OBS-03] Sensitive data MUST be redacted in all observability outputs.
  [AI-OBS-04] Observability data MUST be classified.
  [AI-OBS-05] Cost and token metrics are required for AI operations.
  [AI-OBS-06] Skill performance metrics drive improvement decisions.
  [AI-OBS-07] Failure taxonomy enables better alerting and analysis.
  [AI-OBS-08] Budget policy is enforced during execution.
  [AI-OBS-09] End-to-end trace links Requirement to Artifact.
  [AI-OBS-10] Root cause analysis traces failures through execution chain.
  [AI-OBS-11] Event ordering is guaranteed per execution_id.
  [AI-OBS-12] Event consumers MUST be idempotent.
  [AI-OBS-13] Correlation ID links workflow; Causation ID links causal chain.
  [AI-OBS-14] Observability feedback loop enables self-improvement with governance.
  [AI-OBS-15] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to any AI observability output.
  [AI-OBS-16] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in AI observability output headers or titles — reserved for human use only.

State: +
